== a missing device is a value (99), not a crash
/dev/cancho-no-such-port at 115200 -> 99
== a device that is not a terminal is refused by tcsetattr
/dev/null at 115200 -> refused (ENODEV or ENOTTY)
== a speed with no rate is refused (EINVAL) before the port is touched
/dev/null at 0 -> 22
/dev/null at -5 -> 22
== Linux: a speed that is not in the table of standard rates
/dev/null at 12345 -> 22
== Linux: a pseudo-terminal takes a standard rate
/dev/ptmx at 9600 -> 0
/dev/ptmx at 115200 -> 0
/dev/ptmx at 1000000 -> 0
== Linux: the speed and the raw flags land on the line (read back with stty)
9600: configure 0, speed 9600, flags ok
115200: configure 0, speed 115200, flags ok
1000000: configure 0, speed 1000000, flags ok
